  "name": "W1 · Road edge and runoff catch (draft)",
  "notes": "Job: catch and slow the runoff along the high road edge and top lip, including the strip that drains west to the road. Zone 3 edge plus sector buffer.\nDoubles as the western green firebreak (see 'Green firebreak – west'): keep it low, green and low-fuel.\nFirst: clear the molasses grass (slash, smother, mulch) before planting.\nVetiver or lemongrass hedge on contour along the lip; half-moon basins and log berms where it is steep.\nKeep a 3 m access strip along the boundary for fire and maintenance.\nRain-fed only: plant at the start of the wet (Dec–Feb), mulch hard.\nPlaced from the 2022 LiDAR (1 m): slope, flow lines and ground light.\nDraft from the 19–20 Oct western high edge plan – adjust on site.",
